  "rule": "Per symbol, the instruction text `asm_listing.RULE` defines. A line ending in `:` is a label; every other line is an instruction. A block is a maximal run of instructions that no label interrupts and that ends at a jump, a `ret` or the end of the symbol. A panic block is a block whose last instruction calls a `core::panicking` function. `instructions` counts every instruction; `outside_panic_blocks` leaves the panic blocks out, so it counts each loop body once and both sides of a branch. A loop is a jump to a label that stands earlier in the symbol; its body is the instructions outside panic blocks from that label through the jump. `added` is `outside_panic_blocks` of the checked form minus that of the current form.",
